Using {da'i} with truth-functional connectives is, of course, dissonant, si=
nce a {da'i} sentence has no truth value.=A0 But we do allow this is some o=
ther cases, so perhaps this is no harm.=A0 While it is true that "I suppose=
" and the like don't generate conditionals in a direct way, the usual reaso=
ns for such suppositions is to consider what would happen if the suppositio=
n were true.=A0 This is a longer task than can be handled in a simple condi=
tional, although the results can be summarized in one -- and usually is.=A0=
 Hence the paragraph marker suggestion (on analogy with the inset or boxing=
 conventions of ordinary logic for reductioand conditional proof).




